window.docContents[150].resolve({"/Incompressible-Fluid-Mechanics/#PDEAtlas--Incompressible-Fluid-Mechanics--Solenoidal-Spaces___-Compactness___-and-Pressure":{"contents":"Weak solutions of the fluid equations live on divergence-free fields, and the\nenergy estimates that control them come from a cancellation that holds only\nthere. The results specialize the weak-compactness theorems of the variational\nchapter and the Bochner constraint theorems of the parabolic chapter to a\nsingle linear constraint.\n\n\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Incompressible Fluid Mechanics","header":"8.3. Solenoidal Spaces, Compactness, and Pressure","id":"/Incompressible-Fluid-Mechanics/#PDEAtlas--Incompressible-Fluid-Mechanics--Solenoidal-Spaces___-Compactness___-and-Pressure"},"/Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives/#PDEAtlas--Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives--Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Sobolev-Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Difference-quotients":{"contents":"For every finite exponent, the global forward theory is complete:\n\n* the difference quotient is a bounded linear operator on the global\n   model;* Sobolev membership gives the standard quotient bound by the corresponding\n  weak derivative;* as the step tends to zero, difference quotients converge strongly to the\n  weak derivative in ;* localization by a compactly supported cutoff transports the estimate to an\n  interior region of a domain.\n\nFor , the converse recovers a weak gradient from uniformly\nbounded local difference quotients, with the same bound. It holds on\narbitrary open domains. Reflexivity supplies a weakly convergent subsequence;\ntesting its limit against smooth compactly supported functions identifies\nthe derivative. The endpoint  cannot be added to this statement:\nbounded difference quotients can describe a function of bounded variation\nwith a jump.\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Sobolev Spaces and Weak Derivatives\u0009Coverage and Open Problems\u0009Sobolev Coverage and Open Problems","header":"4.6.1.7. Difference quotients","id":"/Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives/#PDEAtlas--Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives--Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Sobolev-Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Difference-quotients"}});